  "summary": "Apache Tomcat - TOCTOU when setting specific permissions for Unix Domain Sockets - Fix for CVE-2026-65183 did not address APR connector",
  "details": "Time-of-check time-of-use (TOCTOU) race condition vulnerability in Apache Tomcat when creating unix domain sockets for the APR/Native connector allows an unauthorised local user to access the unix domain socket. The fix for CVE-2026-65183 only addressed the NIO connector. It did not address the same issue in the APR/Native connector.\n\n\n\nThis issue affects Apache Tomcat: from 9.0.47 through 9.0.122.\n\n\n\nUsers are recommended to upgrade to version 9.0.123, which fixes the issue.",
